Appendix: Stability of linear DDEs using the Lambert W function  

将从公式（5）中提出的扰动解代入公式（2），并保留到线性项，得到以下线性DDE  

$$
\frac { \mathrm { d } \boldsymbol { \eta } ( u ) } { \mathrm { d } u } = \mathbf { A } \cdot \boldsymbol { \eta } ( u ) + \mathbf { A _ { d } } \cdot \boldsymbol { \eta } ( u - 1 ) ,
$$  

where $\eta(u)$ is the perturbation vector, while $\mathbf{A}$ and $\mathbf{A_d}$ are $N \times N$ coefficient matrices. Matrix $\mathbf{A}$ is proportional to the identity matrix  

$$
\mathbf { A } = - \kappa \left( \cos ( \Delta \phi + \Omega ) + \cos ( \Delta \phi - \Omega ) \right) \cdot \mathbf { 1 } _ { N } \, ,
$$  

# 文本翻译  

而矩阵 $A_{\mathrm{\~d\~}}$ 是形如循环矩阵的矩阵。  

$$
\mathbf { A _ { d } } = \kappa \cdot \left( \begin{array} { c c c c c c } { 0 } & { \cos ( \Delta \phi - \Omega ) } & { 0 } & { \ldots } & { 0 } & { \cos ( \Delta \phi + \Omega ) } \\ { \cos ( \Delta \phi + \Omega ) } & { 0 } & { \cos ( \Delta \phi - \Omega ) } & { \ldots } & { 0 } & { 0 } \\ { 0 } & { \cos ( \Delta \phi + \Omega ) } & { 0 } & { \ldots } & { 0 } & { 0 } \\ { \vdots } & { \vdots } & { \vdots } & { \ddots } & { \vdots } & { \vdots } \\ { 0 } & { 0 } & { 0 } & { \ldots } & { 0 } & { \cos ( \Delta \phi - \Omega ) } \\ { \cos ( \Delta \phi - \Omega ) } & { 0 } & { 0 } & { \ldots } & { \cos ( \Delta \phi + \Omega ) } & { 0 } \end{array} \right) ,
$$  

其中$\mathbf{1}_{N}$是$N \times N$的单位矩阵。方程 (A.1)是一组线性时滞微分方程。对于满足延迟项和非延迟项矩阵的交换的系统，解是已知的 [2]。在我们的案例中，$\mathbf{A}$和$\mathbf{A}_{\mathrm{d}}$的交换是成立的，因为$\mathbf{A}$与单位矩阵成比例。因此解可表示为:  

$$
\eta ( u ) = \sum _ { k = - \infty } ^ { + \infty } \mathrm { e } ^ { [ \mathbf { W } _ { k } ( \mathbf { A } _ { \mathrm { d } } \mathrm { e } ^ { - \mathbf { A } } ) + \mathbf { A } ] u } \mathbf { c } _ { k } ^ { I }
$$  

矩阵$\mathbf{W}_{k}$是矩阵Lambert W函数的第k个分支 [23]，而向量$\mathbf{c}_{k}^{I}$则依赖于系数矩阵、初始条件以及延迟系统的历史。通常，为了确定稳定性，我们需要计算方括号内指数的最大特征值，涵盖所有k的取值。由于Lambert W函数具有无穷多个分支，线性解的特征谱也是无穷的。对于标量系统，与式（2）相反，$k=0$的主分支提供了最右侧的特征值。幸运的是，对于系数矩阵对易的DDE系统，上述陈述也成立 [2]。包含主分支的术语如下所示:  

$$
\eta _ { 0 } ( u ) = \mathrm { e } ^ { [ \mathbf { W } _ { 0 } ( \mathbf { A } _ { \mathrm { d } } \mathrm { e } ^ { - \mathbf { A } } ) + \mathbf { A } ] u } \mathbf { c } _ { 0 } ^ { I }
$$  

为了方便计算矩阵指数，我们需要将指数对角化。首先，我们有一个Lambert W函数参数中的矩阵指数，由于矩阵A是对角矩阵，所以可以很容易地计算:  

$$
\mathrm { e } ^ { - \mathbf { A } } = \mathrm { e } ^ { 2 \kappa \cos ( \Delta \phi ) \cos ( \Omega ) } \cdot \mathbf { 1 } _ { N } .
$$  

因此，矩阵 Lambert W 函数的参数得到简化，仅为一个矩阵与一个标量的乘积。  

$$
\mathbf { W } _ { 0 } ( \mathbf { A } _ { \mathrm { d } } \mathrm { e } ^ { - \mathbf { A } } ) = \mathbf { W } _ { 0 } ( \mathrm { e } ^ { 2 \kappa _ { c } } \mathbf { A } _ { \mathrm { d } } ) ,
$$  

As a result of the above observations, for a random ensemble of initial states and a given parameter set the calculation of the $|\sigma|$ and $|\delta|$ values could help us in estimating the expected attraction basin sizes.  

Finally, please note that our system is deterministic, so a probabilistic approach on the basin sizes should not be necessary, nevertheless the presence of time delay shifts the problem in the realm of infinite-dimensional systems [32], which limits the predictability of the dynamics. The $N$-dimensional phase space also looses its traditional meaning, since the $\theta_{i}$ values are not enough for a complete definition of a state in the phase space, the state histories are also needed.  

# VI. CONCLUSIONS & OUTLOOK  

We studied symmetric phase locked states in rings of locally coupled Kuramoto rotators, interacting through time-delayed coupling. By symmetric phase-locked states we imply that a constant phase difference is allowed between neighboring oscillators. Former studies of such locally coupled systems determined a stability criterion for only a limited number of such states [14, 15]. An implicit stability condition is derived for all the states with constant phase difference. In order to understand the statistics for the selection of the stable stationary states, the attraction basins were investigated by considering large ensembles of uniformly distributed random initial states. Our numerical results show, that the size of the attraction basins can vary between several orders of magnitudes as a function of the parameters. This leads to the situation where stable stationary states are practically unobservable from random initial conditions due to their almost negligible attraction domain. By considering simple symmetry arguments we conjecture heuristic rules regarding the relative sizes of the attraction basins. During our numerical studies, in agreement with [32], we also observed that the presence of time-delay may often lead to the destabilization of simple fixpoint attractors, allowing the emergence of more complex dynamical behaviors besides these phase locked states. Searching for different types of attractors in locally coupled time-delayed systems of oscillators should be thus another objective for future studies.  

